---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pageKey: platforms
navKey: chatbots
title: "Chatbot benchmark — Citere"
description: "How eight public AI assistants handle documented false claims about Ukraine: repeat-rate and source contamination per assistant, with the claims each repeated."
pagination:
  data: build.languages
  alias: lang
  size: 1
permalink: "{{ '/platforms/' | loc(lang) }}"
---
{%- from "partials/bot-mark.njk" import botMark -%}
{%- set doc = copy.en.platforms -%}
<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="{{ '/' | url }}">Home</a> /
  {%- if navigation.has.benchmarks %} <a href="{{ '/benchmarks/' | url }}">Benchmarks</a> / {% endif %}
  <span aria-current="page">Chatbots</span></nav>
<div class="phead"><h1>{{ doc.data.h1 }}</h1>
  <p class="plead">{{ doc.data.lead | fill(figures) | mdInline | safe }}</p></div>

<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Assistants ranked by their worst market on the P2 topical-news persona</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">#</th><th scope="col">{{ 'col.chatbot' | t }}</th><th scope="col">{{ 'col.company' | t }}</th>
    <th scope="col">Worst market</th><th scope="col">{{ 'col.repeatRate' | t }}</th><th scope="col">{{ 'col.contamination' | t }}</th>
    <th scope="col">{{ 'col.claimsRepeated' | t }}</th><th scope="col">{{ 'col.countermeasures' | t }}</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for bot in profiles.chatbots %}
    <tr data-persona="{{ bot.persona }}">
      <td class="num" style="color:var(--dimmer)">{{ loop.index }}</td>
      <td class="cl"><span class="markcell">{{ botMark(logos, bot.key, "sm", true) }}<a href="{{ bot.url | url }}">{{ bot.name }}</a></span></td>
      <td style="color:var(--dim)">{{ bot.company }}</td>
      <td>{% if bot.worst %}{{ bot.worst.name }} <span style="color:var(--dimmer)">{{ bot.worst.language | upper }}</span>{% else %}<span style="color:var(--dimmer)">no market clears n={{ metrics.lowN }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if bot.worst %}<span class="cellstat">{{ bot.worst.headline.repeat_rate.rate | rate }}<small>{{ bot.worst.headline.repeat_rate.ci | ciLabel }} &middot; n={{ bot.worst.headline.repeat_rate.n }}</small></span>{% else %}&mdash;{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if bot.worst %}<span class="cellstat">{{ bot.worst.headline.contamination_rate.rate | rate }}<small>{{ bot.worst.headline.contamination_rate.ci | ciLabel }} &middot; n={{ bot.worst.headline.contamination_rate.n }}</small></span>{% else %}&mdash;{% endif %}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ bot.claimsRepeated }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ bot.countermeasures | length }}</td>
    </tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>

<p class="note">Both figures are the P2 topical-news persona in the market where this assistant does
  worst, with the market named: markets are compared, never merged, and personas are never averaged.
  Contamination is the share of answers that cited a watchlisted domain. The two measure different
  failures and do not move together. We test the public consumer interface, not the API; results
  describe that product at that date and model version.</p>

<div class="exports" style="margin-bottom:44px">
  {%- if navigation.has.benchmarks %}<a href="{{ '/benchmarks/' | url }}">{{ 'action.allBenchmarks' | t }}</a><span>&middot;</span>{% endif %}
  <a href="{{ '/methodology/' | url }}">How repeat-rate is computed</a></div>
